# Inventory Management API - Postman Collection Documentation

## Base URL

```
http://localhost:3000
```

---

# Supplier Requests

## 1. Create Supplier

Method:

```
POST
```

Endpoint:

```
/api/suppliers
```

Body:

```json
{
  "name": "Tech World Suppliers",
  "contactEmail": "techworld@supplier.com"
}
```

Expected Response:

```
201 Created
```

---

# Product Requests

## 2. Create Product

Method:

```
POST
```

Endpoint:

```
/api/products
```

Body:

```json
{
  "name": "Gaming Keyboard",
  "sku": "GK-001",
  "price": 120,
  "stockQuantity": 8,
  "reorderThreshold": 10,
  "supplierId": "supplier_object_id"
}
```

Expected Response:

```
201 Created
```

---

## 3. Get All Products

Method:

```
GET
```

Endpoint:

```
/api/products
```

Expected Response:

```
200 OK
```

---

## 4. Get Product By ID

Method:

```
GET
```

Endpoint:

```
/api/products/:id
```

Example:

```
/api/products/6a74858b77d3823b95a14790
```

Expected Response:

```
200 OK
```

---

## 5. Get Low Stock Products

Method:

```
GET
```

Endpoint:

```
/api/products/low-stock
```

Expected Response:

```
200 OK
```

Returns products where:

```
stockQuantity <= reorderThreshold
```

---

## 6. Update Product

Method:

```
PUT
```

Endpoint:

```
/api/products/:id
```

Body:

```json
{
  "price": 150,
  "stockQuantity": 20
}
```

Expected Response:

```
200 OK
```

---

## 7. Delete Product

Method:

```
DELETE
```

Endpoint:

```
/api/products/:id
```

Expected Response:

```
200 OK
```

---

# Order Requests

## 8. Create Order

Method:

```
POST
```

Endpoint:

```
/api/orders
```

Body:

```json
{
  "productId": "product_object_id",
  "quantity": 4
}
```

Successful Response:

```
201 Created
```

The product stock decreases automatically.

---

## 9. Insufficient Stock Test

Example:

Product stock:

```
2
```

Request:

```json
{
  "productId": "product_object_id",
  "quantity": 5
}
```

Expected Response:

```
409 Conflict
```

Response:

```json
{
  "message": "Insufficient stock"
}
```

---

# Restock Requests

## 10. Create Restock

Method:

```
POST
```

Endpoint:

```
/api/restock
```

Body:

```json
{
  "productId": "product_object_id",
  "supplierId": "supplier_object_id",
  "quantity": 10
}
```

Expected Response:

```
201 Created
```

Product stock increases automatically.

---

## 11. Get Restock History

Method:

```
GET
```

Endpoint:

```
/api/restock
```

Expected Response:

```
200 OK
```

